# DATAD — Give Dax persistent state (the "memory layer" sprint)

You are working in /Users/Shared/DATAD, a Node/Express + MongoDB (Mongoose) +
React/Vite app called DATAD — a student operating system for Indian students.
Its AI assistant is called Dax and lives in `server/ai/`.

## Repo rules you MUST follow

- This repo has a knowledge graph. Before reading/grepping source files, orient
  with `graphify query "<question>"`, `graphify explain "<concept>"`, or
  `graphify path "<A>" "<B>"`. Read `graphify-out/GRAPH_REPORT.md` only for
  broad architecture review.
- After modifying code, run `graphify update .` to keep the graph current.
- Do not commit or push unless I explicitly ask.

## The problem (verified against the working tree, but RE-VERIFY before acting)

Dax computes a deep, per-student understanding on every request and then
throws it away. Concretely:

1. `server/ai/intelligence-layer/index.js` → `buildStudentProfile(userId)` runs
   9 collectors in parallel (identity, memory, tasks, notes, planner, career,
   learning, activity, stress), computes 12 scores via
   `intelligence-layer/scoringEngine.js`, assembles a profile in
   `intelligence-layer/profileFactory.js`, returns it in memory — and **nothing
   persists it**. `grep -rl "intelligenceScore" server/models/` returns nothing.
   There is no snapshot collection. It is recomputed from scratch per request.

2. `server/ai/recommendation-engine/learningLoop.js` learns which recommendation
   generators a student dismisses and adjusts weights — into an in-memory
   `const _overrides = new Map()` (~line 24). Wiped on every restart and every
   deploy. Its own comment says "In a future version these will be persisted."

3. `server/schedulers/index.js` registers ~20 cron jobs (news, market, daily
   case, briefing, reflection, reminders, streaks). **None** snapshots the
   profile, and nothing records or resolves Dax's predictions.

The consequence: the "temporal", "prediction", and "feedback-loop" moats
described in `docs/qwen-context/STUDENT_INTELLIGENCE_GRAPH.md` §29 have code
written for them but no storage behind them. Dax is amnesiac by construction.

**Snapshot data cannot be backfilled.** Every day without a snapshot is student
history permanently lost. That is why Phase 1 is urgent even at low user counts.

### Phase 0 — verify first, then report before you build

Confirm each of the three claims above against the current tree. If any is
already fixed or was inaccurate, say so plainly and adjust the plan rather than
implementing something redundant. Then give me a short plan and proceed.

---

## Conventions you must match

- **Models**: `server/models/*.js`, Mongoose, CommonJS. Use the existing
  re-registration guard pattern seen in `server/ai/embeddings/vectorStore.js`:
  `mongoose.models.X || mongoose.model('X', schema)`. Add indexes explicitly.
- **Cron jobs**: implement the job under `server/automation/<area>/<name>.js`
  exporting a named function, wrap the body in `runJob(...)` from
  `server/automation/jobRunner.js` (see
  `server/automation/briefing/generateDailyBriefing.js` for the reference
  pattern, including the "already exists for today — skipping" idempotency
  guard). Register it in `server/schedulers/index.js` inside `register()` using
  the existing `safe(name, fn)` wrapper.
- **Schedules**: add the cron expression to `cfg.schedules` in
  `server/config/automation.js` with a `process.env.CRON_*` override and a
  sensible default, matching the style of the entries already there. Note
  server time is UTC and the users are in IST — comment the IST equivalent.
- **Tests**: Jest, in `server/tests/`. `tests/setup/blockExternalCalls.js` and
  `tests/socketGuard.js` run as setup — **tests must not make network calls or
  open sockets.** Follow the mocking style of the existing tests.
- **No new AI providers, no new LLM calls** unless a phase explicitly needs one.
  Most of this work is deterministic and should stay that way.

## Exact score keys (from scoringEngine.js — verify)

`currentFocus` (string), `currentChallenges` (string[]), `recommendedTone`
(string), `recommendedResponseLength` (string), `recommendedExamples`
(string[]), `urgencyLevel`, `motivationLevel`, `confidence`,
`learningVelocity`, `careerReadiness`, `contextQualityScore`,
`intelligenceScore` (all 0–100 numbers).

